1
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:32,399
Expect the impossible.

2
00:08:52,799 --> 00:08:58,799
Mission: Impossible is a adventure, action,
thriller film directed by Brian De Palma.

3
00:13:19,199 --> 00:13:25,199
When Ethan Hunt, the leader of a crack espionage team whose perilous operation has gone awry with no explanation,
discovers that a mole has penetrated the CIA, he's surprised to learn that he's the prime suspect.

4
00:17:45,599 --> 00:17:51,599
To clear his name, Hunt now must ferret out the real double
agent and, in the process, even the score.

5
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Ethan Hunt, played by Tom Cruise.

6
00:26:38,399 --> 00:26:44,399
Jim Phelps, played by Jon Voight.

7
00:31:04,799 --> 00:31:10,799
Claire, played by Emmanuelle Béart.

8
00:35:31,199 --> 00:35:37,199
Kittridge, played by Henry Czerny.

9
00:39:57,599 --> 00:40:03,599
Krieger, played by Jean Reno.

10
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Luther, played by Ving Rhames.

11
00:48:50,399 --> 00:48:56,399
Mission: Impossible is a 1996 American spy film directed by Brian De Palma, and produced by and starring Tom
Cruise from a screenplay by David Koepp and Robert Towne and story by Koepp and Steven Zaillian.

12
00:53:16,799 --> 00:53:22,799
A reboot of the 1966 television series of the same name and its 1988 sequel series,
it is the first installment in the Mission: Impossible film series.

13
00:57:43,199 --> 00:57:49,199
It also stars Jon Voight, Henry Czerny, Emmanuelle Béart, Jean Reno,
Ving Rhames, Kristin Scott Thomas, and Vanessa Redgrave.

14
01:02:09,599 --> 01:02:15,599
In the film, Ethan Hunt (Cruise) seeks to uncover who framed him for the
murders of most of his Impossible Missions Force (IMF) team.

15
01:06:35,999 --> 01:06:41,999
Numerous efforts by Paramount Pictures to create a film adaptation of the television series stalled until Cruise
founded Cruise/Wagner Productions in 1992 and decided on Mission: Impossible as its inaugural project.

16
01:11:02,399 --> 01:11:08,399
Development initially began with filmmaker Sydney Pollack but most of the final screenplay was completed after De Palma, Steven Zaillian, David
Koepp and Robert Towne were hired; De Palma also designed most of the action sequences, while Cruise did most of his own stunts.

17
01:15:28,799 --> 01:15:34,799
Principal photography began in March 1995 and lasted until that August, with filming locations
including London, Pinewood Studios in England, and Prague (a rarity in Hollywood at the time).

18
01:19:55,199 --> 01:20:01,199
Mission: Impossible was theatrically released in the United
States by Paramount Pictures on May 22, 1996.

19
01:24:21,599 --> 01:24:27,599
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with praise for the action sequences, De
Palma's direction and Cruise's performance, but criticism for a convoluted plot.

20
01:28:48,000 --> 01:28:54,000
The film grossed $457.7 million worldwide, making it the third-highest-grossing film of
1996, while the dance rendition of the original theme song by Larry Mullen Jr.

21
01:33:14,399 --> 01:33:20,399
and Adam Clayton became a top-ten hit internationally and was nominated
for the Grammy Award for Best Pop Instrumental Performance.

22
01:37:40,799 --> 01:37:46,799
The film's success led to a long-running film franchise, beginning with
Mission: Impossible 2, released four years later in 2000.

23
01:42:07,199 --> 01:42:13,199
The film explores themes of mask, mission, london, england,
central intelligence agency (cia), computer.

24
01:46:33,599 --> 01:46:39,599
The tone is intense.
